\title{Session tables must start small: with tables of 1 to 2 MiB every probe was a cache miss}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\meta{origin}{rlvm-machine/NOTES-INT.md}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: deviation I1 of [rep-machine-INT](rep-machine-INT), the notes of the integration of the machine; [the session on the machine](ses-Z72N). Native image in the arena container, one worker, the plain machine.}
\table{
\tr{\th{Base sizes of a session}\th{Init}\th{Cedar slice}\th{Std}}
\tr{\td{as in the instruction-set document: 2^18 records, 2^19 table slots, 2^20 run words}\td{13.54 s}\td{3.98 s}\td{21.79 s}}
\tr{\td{based on 2^12 records}\td{10.11 s}\td{3.84 s}\td{16.18 s}}
\tr{\td{based on 2^14 records, the choice}\td{9.27 s}\td{3.70 s}\td{15.80 s}}
\tr{\td{based on 2^16 records}\td{9.26 s}\td{3.74 s}\td{15.39 s}}
}
\ul{
\li{A declaration of Init makes about 860 records. Tables sized for a large declaration are mostly empty and far larger than the cache, so every probe missed.}
\li{The owner of the store had measured the direction; the integrator changed the sizes and kept the sizes of the design document behind a property for sweeps.}
\li{The same reasoning later set [the session cap](ins-FJ5R): the right size of the tables of the machine is a property of the processor cache.}
}
\p{A third of the CPU time of the plain machine on Init was a sizing constant. It was found from a profile, not from a count of steps, which the sizes do not change.}
\p{See also: [the value model](design-value-model).}
